item.text:
{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q010_rossmann_family_function_divergence","answer":"In stable SCOPe 2.08, these are three distinct families within the same NAD(P)-binding Rossmann-fold superfamily (SUNID 51735, SCCS c.2.1): alcohol dehydrogenase-like C-terminal domains are c.2.1.1 (SUNID 51736), CoA-binding domains are c.2.1.8 (SUNID 51900), and potassium-channel NAD-binding domains are c.2.1.9 (SUNID 63944). All also share fold c.2 (SUNID 51734), whose annotated core is a three-layer α/β/α structure with a six-stranded parallel β-sheet in order 321456. The shared superfamily—not merely the fold—means SCOPe supports probable common ancestry of their classified domains; their separation into families represents substantial divergence and makes within-family relationships closer than the relationships among these three families.

This does not license functional interchange. Alcohol-dehydrogenase reaction chemistry or substrate specificity must not be transferred to the CoA-binding or channel-associated families; CoA binding or synthetase chemistry must not be transferred to the others; and NAD/NADP preference, ligand affinity, potassium-channel gating, ion selectivity, regulation, or membrane-protein function must not be inferred for the other families. SCOPe classifies domains, not entire multidomain proteins. In particular, c.2.1.1 carries the comment that the N-terminal all-beta domain defines the family, emphasizing the importance of domain context, while the c.2.1.9 annotation is an automated mapping to Pfam PF02254—not independent experimental validation and not evidence of low quality.

A structure from another family may be a remote-homology template for the conserved Rossmann core, but it is not automatically an interchangeable template for ligand geometry, active sites, family-specific insertions, oligomerization, or channel coupling. Stronger functional or mechanistic conclusions require domain-aware sequence/profile alignments and phylogenetic evidence, global structural alignment with residue correspondence, compatible domain architecture, ligand-bound structures, biochemical binding/enzymology data, and—for channel claims—electrophysiological or gating experiments. No representative can be ranked from the hierarchy: candidate templates would require matched coverage and biological state plus candidate-specific ASTRAL/SPACI or AEROSPACI, resolution, R-factor, and validation evidence.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","scop-homology/references/biological-interpretation.md","scop-homology/references/api-usage.md","MCP tools: mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info; mcp__scope__search_scop; mcp__scope__get_scop_node","mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info: /api/v1/releases/current","mcp__scope__search_scop: /api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=alcohol+dehydrogenase&mode=token&limit=50; /api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=CoA-binding&mode=auto&limit=50; /api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=potassium+channel&mode=auto&limit=50","mcp__scope__get_scop_node: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736/homology; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900/homology; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944/homology; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2